Start the sample todo service

A small HTTP service that keeps a list of todos in memory.
-- .gitignore --
node_modules/
-- README.md --
# marshal-sample

A small todo service to try Marshal on. It is safe to try things on: Marshal made this copy for
you, nothing else uses it, and removing the project from Marshal never deletes it.

## Run it

It needs Node.js 22.18 or newer, and nothing else to install.

    npm run dev

The server listens on http://localhost:3000. It keeps the todos in memory, so they dissapear
when the server stops.

## What it does

- `GET /todos` lists the todos.
- `POST /todos` adds one. Send `{"title": "Buy milk"}`.
-- package.json --
{
  "name": "marshal-sample",
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "private": true,
  "description": "A small todo service to try Marshal on.",
  "type": "module",
  "engines": {
    "node": ">=22.18"
  },
  "scripts": {
    "dev": "node --watch src/server.ts",
    "start": "node src/server.ts"
  }
}
-- tsconfig.json --
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2023",
    "module": "NodeNext",
    "moduleResolution": "NodeNext",
    "strict": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
